        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2017",
        "question_text": "<p>Express $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x - 1)(x + 2)}$ in partial fractions.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Assume $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x - 1)(x + 2)} = \\frac{A}{x - 1} + \\frac{B}{x + 2}$.<br>Multiply through by $(x - 1)(x + 2)$: $3x + 5 = A(x + 2) + B(x - 1)$.<br>Solve for $A$ and $B$ by substituting $x = 1$ and $x = -2$: <br>For $x = 1$: $3(1) + 5 = A(3) \\Rightarrow A = \\frac{8}{3}$.<br>For $x = -2$: $3(-2) + 5 = B(-3) \\Rightarrow B = \\frac{1}{3}$.<br>Thus, $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x - 1)(x + 2)} = \\frac{8/3}{x - 1} + \\frac{1/3}{x + 2}$.</p>",
